WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.849
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level two.

2
00:00:06.149 --> 00:00:09.989
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.289 --> 00:00:16.923
Unit twenty-one: The Tourism Economy. Today you will use inversion for emphasis: not only ... but also.

4
00:00:17.223 --> 00:00:20.050
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.977
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.817 --> 00:00:25.609
Tourism.

7
00:00:26.617 --> 00:00:30.276
Tourism means the business of providing services for travellers.

8
00:00:30.883 --> 00:00:33.452
Tourism is a major industry in Cambodia.

9
00:00:34.050 --> 00:00:36.609
Your turn. Say: Tourism.

10
00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:40.270
Tourism.

11
00:00:41.017 --> 00:00:42.029
Visitors.

12
00:00:43.017 --> 00:00:46.537
Visitors means people who travel to a place for a short time.

13
00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:49.475
Millions of visitors arrive each year.

14
00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:52.573
Your turn. Say: Visitors.

15
00:00:55.433 --> 00:00:56.516
Visitors.

16
00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:58.251
Hotel.

17
00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:02.225
Hotel means a building where travellers pay to stay.

18
00:01:02.817 --> 00:01:05.478
The new hotel employs one hundred workers.

19
00:01:06.083 --> 00:01:08.573
Your turn. Say: Hotel.

20
00:01:11.433 --> 00:01:12.620
Hotel.

21
00:01:13.383 --> 00:01:14.303
Jobs.

22
00:01:15.317 --> 00:01:18.164
Jobs means paid work for which people are employed.

23
00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:21.585
Tourism creates jobs for guides and drivers.

24
00:01:22.183 --> 00:01:24.801
Your turn. Say: Jobs.

25
00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:28.726
Jobs.

26
00:01:29.483 --> 00:01:30.333
Revenue.

27
00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:34.569
Revenue means the money a business or government receives.

28
00:01:35.183 --> 00:01:37.380
Tourist revenue rose by ten percent.

29
00:01:37.983 --> 00:01:40.032
Your turn. Say: Revenue.

30
00:01:42.867 --> 00:01:43.810
Revenue.

31
00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:45.470
Season.

32
00:01:46.483 --> 00:01:49.992
Season means a period of the year when something typically happens.

33
00:01:50.583 --> 00:01:53.012
The dry season brings the most visitors.

34
00:01:53.617 --> 00:01:56.037
Your turn. Say: Season.

35
00:01:58.900 --> 00:01:59.773
Season.

36
00:02:00.517 --> 00:02:01.727
Heritage site.

37
00:02:02.717 --> 00:02:06.121
Heritage site means a place of historic or cultural importance.

38
00:02:06.717 --> 00:02:09.250
A heritage site needs careful protection.

39
00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:12.746
Your turn. Say: Heritage site.

40
00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:16.845
Heritage site.

41
00:02:17.583 --> 00:02:18.503
Economy.

42
00:02:19.517 --> 00:02:23.107
Economy means the system of money, trade and jobs in a country.

43
00:02:23.717 --> 00:02:26.459
The economy depends on tourism and garments.

44
00:02:27.050 --> 00:02:29.412
Your turn. Say: Economy.

45
00:02:32.267 --> 00:02:33.256
Economy.

46
00:02:34.067 --> 00:02:37.729
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:38.583 --> 00:02:45.647
Visal, an article says 'Not only does tourism create jobs, but it also brings revenue.' Why does 'does' come before 'tourism'?

48
00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:55.716
After 'not only' at the start of a sentence, we invert the subject and auxiliary, as in a question: not only does tourism create...

49
00:02:56.817 --> 00:02:57.969
Is it common?

50
00:02:59.083 --> 00:03:09.354
In formal writing, yes. 'Not only did visitors fill the hotels, but they also supported local guides.' It gives strong emphasis.

51
00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.368
What are the risks of tourism?

52
00:03:13.483 --> 00:03:21.941
Rarely does growth come without cost. A heritage site may be damaged, and the economy may depend on one season.

53
00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:24.809
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:30.111
Grammar focus: Inversion: not only  but also; rarely and seldom.

55
00:03:30.411 --> 00:03:31.470
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:32.183 --> 00:03:35.820
Not only does tourism create jobs, but it also brings revenue.

57
00:03:36.717 --> 00:03:41.247
Not only did visitors fill hotels, but they also supported local guides.

58
00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:44.533
Rarely does growth come without cost.

59
00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:54.037
After Not only / Rarely / Seldom at the start, invert the subject and auxiliary: Not only does it..., Rarely did they... Use 'but also' for the second part.

60
00:03:54.783 --> 00:03:59.084
Be careful! Don't say: Not only tourism creates jobs.

61
00:04:01.033 --> 00:04:04.171
Say: Not only does tourism create jobs.

62
00:04:04.471 --> 00:04:06.610
Invert the subject and auxiliary.

63
00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.971
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:12.430
Tourism and the Economy.

65
00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:15.588
Tourism is a pillar of many national economies.

66
00:04:16.600 --> 00:04:22.872
Not only does it create jobs for hotel staff and guides, but it also brings revenue to small towns.

67
00:04:23.867 --> 00:04:28.850
Rarely do visitors realise how much a single season can matter to a family's income.

68
00:04:29.833 --> 00:04:33.714
However, a heritage site that receives too many visitors may be damaged.

69
00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:38.081
Balanced tourism therefore protects both people and places.

70
00:04:39.167 --> 00:04:43.273
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:44.117 --> 00:04:47.939
Not only blank tourism create jobs, but it also brings revenue.

72
00:04:48.239 --> 00:04:51.567
A, does. B, is. C, do.

73
00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:57.098
The answer is A: does.

74
00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:00.795
A place of historic importance is a blank site.

75
00:05:01.095 --> 00:05:04.354
A, heritage. B, season. C, revenue.

76
00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:10.143
The answer is A: heritage.

77
00:05:11.283 --> 00:05:13.910
The money a business or government receives is blank.

78
00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:18.095
A, revenue. B, tourism. C, hotel.

79
00:05:21.633 --> 00:05:23.668
The answer is A: revenue.

80
00:05:24.817 --> 00:05:26.619
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:26.919 --> 00:05:33.986
A, Rarely growth does come free.. B, Rarely does growth come free.. C, Rarely growth comes does free..

82
00:05:37.533 --> 00:05:40.764
The answer is B: Rarely does growth come free..

83
00:05:41.917 --> 00:05:46.110
According to the reading, balanced tourism protects both people and…

84
00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:50.517
A, places. B, hotels only. C, seasons.

85
00:05:54.067 --> 00:05:55.915
The answer is A: places.

86
00:05:57.100 --> 00:06:00.101
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:03.890
How does tourism help or harm local communities?

88
00:06:12.683 --> 00:06:14.311
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:14.611 --> 00:06:38.016
Tourism helps communities by creating jobs and bringing revenue to hotels, shops and farms. Not only does it support families, but it also encourages the protection of heritage. However, it can harm a place if too many visitors damage a heritage site, raise prices or crowd out local people. Good planning is therefore essential.

90
00:06:38.316 --> 00:06:39.979
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:06:40.883 --> 00:06:47.146
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and inversion: not only  but also; rarely and seldom.

92
00:06:47.446 --> 00:06:52.084
Today's value is sustainable thinking. Choose what can last for the long term.

93
00:06:52.384 --> 00:06:55.350
See you in Unit twenty-two. Goodbye!

94
00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:58.709
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

